WEBVTT

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.790
Certainly glad you could join me again today.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:34.880
Got your palette set up, let's get going here.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.800
Let's start off and have them graphically run

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.120
all the colors across the screen

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.740
that you need to do this painting with me.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.160
And they'll come across, as usual,

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.940
in the same order that I have them on the palette,

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.560
starting with the white and working around.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.600
While they're doing that, let's go on up here.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:48.400
I've already covered the canvas

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.020
with a thin, even coat of liquid white.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.740
It's nice and wet and slick and all ready to go.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:56.080
I thought maybe today, let's do a little fall scene

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.200
where maybe the weather's not too great.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.880
You know, in the fall, we have a lot of rainy.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.400
weather and you know the snow's gonna come pretty soon.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.960
So let's do something like that and just have some fun.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.030
I'm gonna start out using a small, small amount

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:12.790
of yellow ochre, just the tiniest little bit,

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:14.470
very small amount.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.620
And right here, sort of make a determination

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:19.120
where the horizon's gonna be.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:22.210
And I'm gonna begin swinging this upward,

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:24.180
just using strokes like so.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.990
Little bit more color, we'll have a little water

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:29.530
in this painting.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.700
As you know, I'm sort of a water fanatic.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:38.880
I like that water, put a little yellow in there, okay?

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.500
I'm gonna go right into some Van Dyke Brown.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.060
In the same way, just tap the brush into it, okay?

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:46.260
Let's go right up here.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.040
And I'm gonna put a little brown right in here.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.680
Beginning to create these sky angles.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.760
Don't let them get too straight like this.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.090
It'll disturb you when it's done.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.990
Now I'm gonna take brown and a touch of Prussian blue.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:05.090
Let me say that again, a touch.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:09.380
Prussian blue is so strong, just a little bit.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:11.780
Just brown and blue, okay.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:17.670
Now then, just begin bringing that all together.

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:21.620
Add a touch of the midnight black to it.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.060
So now we have, in the sky,

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:28.460
we have a little bit of yellow ochre, some brown.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.330
A little Prussian blue and some midnight black.

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:36.790
We're just gonna sort of work all these

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.280
nice little colors together.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:40.740
Try to keep the blue off that yellow

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.120
or you'll get a bright green sky.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.520
Okay, now then, before we start blending that,

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.800
we still have a dirty old brush,

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:51.260
and we'll take some more of the Prussian blue,

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:56.150
a little bit of the black, there you go,

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:57.980
and let's go ahead and lay our water in.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:02:59.340
Pull from the outside in.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:04.400
See, if you start from here and go across,

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:05.180
watch what happens.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:06.660
You touch here and go across,

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.560
you get this big line, that's bad.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:10.140
And then it's hard to blend out.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.620
So start from the outside and come over,

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.840
and that way you don't have that harsh line

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:15.940
that you have to blend out.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:21.030
Little tricks like that save you a lot of agony.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:23.800
We want this to be easy and we want it to work for you.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:29.190
Okay, a little bit more of the midnight black

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:29.970
and prussian blue.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.670
You don't want to kill all that nice little yellow area

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:38.190
that you have, because that blue and black

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:39.920
will eat it up in a heartbeat.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:44.350
A little darker at the bottom than it is at the top.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:47.470
That'll help create your illusion of distance.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.380
Okay, let me wash the old brush.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.240
Wash the old brush.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.480
Shake off the excess.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.300
That is the fun part.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:03.880
Okay, let's go right back up here.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.510
Now I'm gonna begin blending this together.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:08.800
Follow the angles in the sky.

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:11.270
I'm gonna use long strokes.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.610
Start in the light area and work up toward the darker area.

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.750
That way your brush is dirty when it gets to the top.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:19.780
Use your clean brush in the light area

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:23.110
and you can just begin bringing all this together.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:25.600
Follow those angles though.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:31.800
Nice and soft.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:37.210
Okay, and that gives us a quick, happy little sky.

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:39.380
Down here, we just go all the way across.

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:42.290
Straightens out the water and brings it all together.

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:47.650
And we're ready.

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:49.750
Let me get an old fan brush here.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:52.740
I'm gonna mix up.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.530
Let's take a little black, a little brown,

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.970
tiny bit of the Prussian blue, and a little

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.370
a little bit of alizarin crimson into that.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.250
Put some white here and pull a little bit of that into it.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.030
Maybe I'll add a little more blue to that.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:14.290
Touch more crimson, there we go.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:15.630
That's sort of what I'm looking for.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:20.130
It's a very dark lavender to the blue side.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.710
Very dark, it's almost a gray color.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:26.560
This is gonna be a gray, cloudy day.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.810
Okay, let me wipe off my knife.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.660
Now, let's take the old fan brush

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:33.570
and go right through a little bit of color.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.450
Don't need a lot of paint on the brush this time,

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:38.620
just a little, add a small amount of brown into that,

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:40.540
a little more into the brownish color.

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:43.550
There we go, good, let's go right up here.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.640
Now, back in here, you have to make a decision.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:50.080
Maybe there lives some happy little evergreens.

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:52.580
Just take the corner of the brush,

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:57.120
just back and forth, just sort of pop in,

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:58.510
just a little evergreen.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.140
some indications of some that are even farther away.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.820
All we see is just the basic shapes.

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:09.150
Just touching and sort of pulling it downward.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.180
Make all kinds of little basic shapes.

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:17.280
See, touch, use the top part of the brush

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:18.780
and just give it a little downward snap.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:22.320
There, paint on the brush.

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:25.290
Maybe over here we got some.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:28.350
Be careful, these will get looking like fence posts.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:35.400
And to about there, that's good enough.

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:42.040
Now then, we'll put a few more indications

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:45.050
of some trees that have a little more shape to them.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:46.670
And we're just using the corner of the brush

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:50.480
and just work them in back and forth.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:54.900
These little trees live right in your fan brush.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.260
Sometimes you have to sort of scare them out.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:04.290
and you just put as many or as few as you want in your world.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:12.980
He's got a little friend there.

00:07:15.170 --> 00:07:15.950
Just drop him in.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:19.600
Now then, I want to create the illusion of mist back here.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.560
I want this to be very soft and very distant,

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:24.450
so we'll take the two-inch brush and tap.

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:26.560
I'm using the top corner.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:28.680
See, look how hard it's hitting, it's bending.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:34.480
Really get in here, and tap it, and tap it.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:42.670
You can create the illusion of very, very soft area

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:47.680
back here, even let it come up above some of these here

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:52.150
to really soften it, these trees are already,

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:53.950
they're already just lost right in the mist.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:03.800
Can you believe how that pushes all that back?

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:08.420
Just that little tapping action, okay?

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:12.680
Now then, let's have another plane in the painting,

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:14.360
and a plane, I mean just another area

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.460
that's closer to you.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.330
So we'll take those same old colors.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.310
We'll use some brown,

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.190
and we'll put some dark sienna in there this time,

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.520
and a little bit of sap green.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:24.520
As things get closer,

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:26.980
we'll begin to see a little more detail.

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:29.300
Just a little sap green, though, okay?

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.060
This brush is really full of paint.

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:33.600
Let's go right up in here, there it is.

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:36.760
These trees are a little closer, they're a little bit bigger.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:40.430
Look at that, turn that old brush over

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:41.650
and use both sides of it.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:45.350
There we go, this tree's stronger.

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:50.630
He's got a little more light, okay?

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:52.220
We don't want him to get lonely,

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:53.520
so we'll give him a friend too.

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:59.980
Friends are so important, not only to trees, but to us.

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:05.470
And through painting, I have made hundreds and hundreds

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:06.970
of new friends all over the country,

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:09.610
and that may be the most rewarding part of all this.

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:12.580
Most rewarding part.

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.430
Here's a happy little tree.

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:19.940
He lives right there.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:23.100
Just sort of visualize in your mind

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.020
where you think a tree would be happy,

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:25.740
and you put him in there.

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:28.910
Just put him in there.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:29.970
Take a look.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:30.920
a little bit of the dark sienna

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:33.570
and just tap it onto this brush

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:35.230
and then I wanna gather up some of this color

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:36.330
that we had on a tree

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:40.450
and begin very softly putting in little hills.

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:43.140
Look at there, see?

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:45.250
Pick up some of that tree color

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:49.360
and just let it just tap, let it go.

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:52.210
There's a tiny bit of dark sienna on the brush.

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:55.500
Tiny bit, tiniest little bit.

00:09:57.110 --> 00:09:59.030
See how you can set those trees right up on a little hill?

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:01.710
and then you begin pulling that down.

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:05.980
But I want this to be very, very soft, very quiet,

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:09.340
very gentle little paintings.

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:12.170
And when you're doing yours at home,

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:13.770
if you want it to be brighter and stronger,

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:15.950
just use a little stronger color,

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:19.410
because painting is a very individual thing.

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:28.960
Okay, now, let's go right back into here and load up,

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:29.960
just a little.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.610
load that fan brush full of paint, okay?

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:35.070
Tell you what let's do.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:37.500
Let's have a tree that lives right there.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:40.720
And we take just the corner of the brush,

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:45.160
working him down.

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:48.960
Then you can just push that old tree

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:49.880
right out of that brush.

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:55.680
Paint, just push it hard when you get down this far.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.520
When you first start, you're pushing quite easy.

00:10:57.700 --> 00:10:59.740
The time you get down here.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.760
Getting tough with it, strong with it, more color.

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:09.040
Okay, tell you what, let's do it right here.

00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:10.870
Big son of a gun.

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:14.980
See, all these different sizes of trees

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:17.600
help create the illusion of distance,

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:18.760
depth in the painting.

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:29.790
It's beginning to look like fall yet, mean.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:39.150
Okay, now then I'm gonna go back into a little tiny,

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:43.360
tiny little bit of that dark sienna, tiny.

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:44.620
Can't say that enough times.

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:47.120
And I'm gonna create another plane here,

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.240
and I'm gonna pick up some of the tree color.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.710
See how that, and all I'm doing is just tapping the canvas.

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:57.840
Just tap, bring it right on across,

00:11:59.200 --> 00:11:59.960
add the least little.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.920
a little touch more of the sienna.

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:05.730
See, it creates a whole other plane

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:07.470
and pushes all those trees back here,

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:09.360
back into the distance.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:13.280
Isn't that super?

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:16.500
I'm gonna have water here,

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:19.820
so let's take a little bit of that color

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:22.000
and just pull it down.

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:23.480
So we have a little reflection.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:26.040
I'm using just a little bit of the dark sienna,

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:27.460
a little Van Dyke brown on the brush

00:12:27.460 --> 00:12:29.980
to pull down and create a reflection.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.570
here, just a happy little reflection there.

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:41.380
And then lightly go across, okay?

00:12:41.850 --> 00:12:43.510
Now then, I'm gonna take the same old brush

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:45.630
without cleaning it, just the same old dirty brush,

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:50.220
tap right into a little bit of the yellow ochre

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:56.230
and the bright red, gently, just tap, okay?

00:12:56.990 --> 00:12:59.150
Now then, here, this is a little closer,

00:12:59.170 --> 00:12:59.970
so we're beginning to...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.530
to see an indication of some highlights.

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:06.690
And same way, just gently, gently tapping.

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:14.620
Bright red and a tiniest little touch of that yellow ochre.

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:16.670
Now the red is very strong.

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.020
Careful with it, careful.

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:22.540
It'll eat up your whole world in just a second.

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:27.220
Take a little brown, a little dark sienna mixed together.

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:29.980
Pull it out, cut across, get that small.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.580
I'll roll a paint right on the edge of the knife.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:38.480
A little land indication right in there.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:46.270
Just sort of scrubbing across the canvas.

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:49.050
Tiniest little bit.

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:53.820
Add a little white to that same color, like that.

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:59.050
Then just an indication of a touch of highlight here.

00:13:59.150 --> 00:13:59.970
I don't want much.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.760
highlight in this, just a touch here and there.

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:07.800
A little bit of the liquid white, cut across it,

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:11.080
and we'll put just an indication of a little water life.

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:14.730
Not too much, not too bright.

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:19.920
Okay, then go back into my brown,

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:22.380
Sienna and the Van Dyke.

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:25.060
I'm gonna grab some more of this tree color.

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:26.920
I'm gonna put a little peninsula.

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:29.530
I think it comes right out here.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:33.670
And when you're doing this, just step back,

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:36.630
look at your painting, and make decisions.

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:39.250
Just make decisions.

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:41.960
Pull a little bit of this color down,

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:48.000
just a little, gently, gently across.

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:50.950
Now, same old dirty brush,

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:54.170
back into my yellow ochre and bright red mixture.

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:57.950
Just a little, same old dirty brush.

00:14:58.870 --> 00:14:59.970
You can get over here and let me...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.500
a little bit of this cad yellow to it, it's all right.

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:07.200
Now, see, follow the angles of the land,

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:12.560
the lay of the land, just follow it right on down.

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:16.080
Brighter on top, and then darker, darker, darker

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:16.860
as it works down.

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:21.310
If you want to show a little protrusion here, see?

00:15:21.510 --> 00:15:23.680
See, how easy that is?

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:26.110
Creates the illusion of another little hill,

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:28.970
just by changing the value of the color, or the intensity.

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:31.840
a little bit of that right down to the water,

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:34.600
go across, and you have instant reflections.

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:37.410
Let's play a little bit over here.

00:15:37.570 --> 00:15:38.330
Tell you what let's do.

